1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,833
The fellow from the feed store

2
00:00:01,933 --> 00:00:03,500
borrowed twelve dollars—

3
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:05,700
and this enamel mug—

4
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,500
the same Tuesday. Returned neither.

5
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:08,600
Three years later,

6
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,367
he brought the mug back,

7
00:00:10,467 --> 00:00:12,467
plus a pie his wife made,

8
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,000
apologizing like he'd misplaced the courthouse.

9
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:17,867
I reached for my little ledger...

10
00:00:18,967 --> 00:00:21,400
then watched his hand shake.

11
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,733
Keeping score tells you what you're owed.

12
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:27,133
It can't tell you what a man is carrying.

13
00:00:27,233 --> 00:00:28,900
So I set the pencil down

14
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,333
and poured him coffee.

15
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:31,867
Funny thing:

16
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,533
the account got lighter before the debt did.

17
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:34,600
What are you carrying

18
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:35,933
just because the ledger says so?
